WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.939
The Game of Thrones books describe hundreds
of years of history – full of kings and

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:12.260
wars, drama and politics, and an awful lot
of incest.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:18.160
Three hundred years ago, Aegon Targaryen took
over Westeros, and his dynasty ruled for almost

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:24.440
three centuries – until Robert Baratheon
took over, and the main series begins.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:29.500
Targaryen rule was often tumultuous – like,
the Targaryens almost destroyed themselves

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.710
in a civil war called the Dance of the Dragons.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.789
But in the hundred years before Robert’s
Rebellion, the greatest threat to House Targaryen

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:40.629
was the Blackfyres.

00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:45.940
King Aegon Targaryen the Fourth was called
“the Unworthy”, cause he was a terrible

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.940
king.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.629
He was corrupt and impulsive, full of gluttony
and lust.

00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:56.179
His wife was his sister Naerys, and they had
a son called Prince Daeron.

00:00:56.179 --> 00:01:03.219
But Aegon also took hundreds of other women
as lovers, and had dozens of bastard children.

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:08.350
Aegon hated Naerys and Daeron, so he spread
rumours that Naerys had cheated on him with

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:12.939
their brother Aemon, and that Aemon was Daeron’s
real father.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:17.770
Aegon threatened to make one of his bastards
heir to the throne instead of Daeron.

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:21.510
Aegon’s favourite bastard was Daemon Waters.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:25.020
His mother was Aegon’s cousin Daena “the
Defiant”.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:31.039
Daena had been locked away to preserve her
innocence from lustful men, but Daena escaped

00:01:31.039 --> 00:01:33.179
and hooked up with Aegon.

00:01:33.179 --> 00:01:38.740
Daena named their son Daemon, after a Prince
Daemon Targaryen who had lived fifty years

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:39.850
earlier.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:46.710
Prince Daemon was renowned as a dangerous
man, “the wonder and the terror of his age”

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:52.640
– so the name was an ominous “warning”
of the man who Daemon Waters would become.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.939
From a young age, Daemon was a talented warrior.

00:01:55.939 --> 00:02:00.890
When he was just twelve years old, King Aegon
made Daemon a knight – and gave him the

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:05.369
legendary Valyrian steel sword Blackfyre.

00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:10.770
Blackfyre was the sword of Aegon the Conqueror,
carried by Targaryen kings for centuries [~180

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:11.770
years].

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.490
It’s a powerful symbol of the Targaryen
throne, and King Aegon gave it not to his

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:20.890
true heir Prince Daeron Targaryen, but to
his bastard son Daemon.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:25.710
From that day, Daemon took the name Daemon
Blackfyre.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:32.250
King Aegon died a horrible death, literally
rotting under the weight of his obesity.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:38.950
And on his deathbed, he made one last spiteful
act – he legitimised all his bastards, giving

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.080
them the right to inherit like a trueborn
child.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.790
Daeron was still his eldest son and heir,
but now his bastards were also in line for

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:52.490
the Throne – a perfect recipe for conflict.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:55.050
After Aegon died, Daeron became king.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:03:00.380
He worked to repair the realm that Aegon had
corrupted, and he tried to keep friendly with

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.380
Aegon’s bastards.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:06.760
He gave Daemon some land, and married him
to a woman called Rohanne of Tyrosh.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:12.340
King Daeron married a Dornish princess, Myriah
Martell, and successfully unified Dorne with

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.360
the rest of Westeros [under Targaryen rule],
which the Targaryens had been trying to do

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.440
since the Conquest.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.270
King Daeron gave the Dornish more political
influence, and Dorne got special rights and

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:28.180
privileges that the other kingdoms didn’t
have – which angered some lords.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:32.040
Houses in the reach and the stormlands [Marcher
lords] had been fighting the Dornish for thousands

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.630
of years, and still saw them as enemies.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:39.360
Aegon the Unworthy had hated the Dornish and
tried to attack them.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:44.600
And before him, tens of thousands died in
a previous war for Dorne.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.180
There was a lot of bad blood here.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:51.830
So when King Daeron got in bed with the Dornish,
some people were angry.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:56.980
Some didn’t trust Daeron and Myriah’s
son, Prince Baelor Breakspear, because he

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:04.180
had the dark hair and dark eyes of a Dornishman,
not the blonde hair and purple eyes of a Targaryen.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:10.200
So a combination of politics and prejudice
turned some lords against King Daeron [and

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.200
his Dornish allies].

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:16.120
They looked instead to Daemon Blackfyre – he
looked like a Targaryen king.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.820
And Daemon was way cooler than Daeron.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:25.830
Daeron was weak and scholarly, he read books
and listened to women, while Daemon was a

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:30.650
big strong warrior with the legendary “sword
of kings”, Blackfyre.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:36.350
Some lords thought “Daemon was the better
man”, and urged him to rebel and take the

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.510
Throne.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:41.260
Daemon was also influenced by his siblings.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:46.560
The “Great Bastards” of Aegon the Unworthy
included Aegor Rivers, called “Bittersteel”,

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:51.570
Brynden Rivers called “Bloodraven”, and
Shiera Seastar.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:57.420
Shiera was the most beautiful woman in the
realm, and supposedly a sorcerer who bathed

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:00.230
in blood to keep her youth.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:05.490
Bittersteel and Bloodraven hated each other,
because they both loved Shiera, and Shiera

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.460
chose Bloodraven over Bittersteel.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:11.690
Bittersteel and Bloodraven also had a family
rivalry.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:17.500
Cause Bittersteel’s mother was Barba Bracken,
and Bloodraven’s mother was Melissa Blackwood,

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:22.160
and the Blackwoods and Brackens have hated
each other for thousands of years.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:27.000
When Barba hooked up with King Aegon, the
Brackens plotted and schemed to tryn make

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:32.160
Barba queen – which could’ve potentially
made Bittersteel heir to the throne.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.530
But that.. went.. very badly, and [partly
because of Daeron] the Brackens lost their

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:38.340
political influence.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:42.980
While Melissa Blackwood and Bloodraven kept
their influence on the throne.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:48.740
So Bittersteel was.. bitter about the fall
of his family, and about Bloodraven getting

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.260
his girl Shiera.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:55.800
Author George Martin said Bittersteel was
“pissed off all his life”, and he hated

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.010
Bloodraven and Daeron.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:04.330
So Bittersteel urged Daemon to rebel against
Daeron, and claim the throne himself.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:09.440
There was also this knight called Quentyn
Ball, nicknamed Fireball – he was angry

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:12.570
at King Daeron for not letting him join the
Kingsguard.

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:18.150
So Fireball and Bittersteel and everyone else
who had beef with Daeron finally convinced

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.470
Daemon to rebel.

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:24.790
Daemon declared himself the rightful king
of Westeros, and the true heir of King Aegon

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:29.180
– claiming that Daeron was the bastard son
of Aegon’s brother.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:34.690
So rebel lords gathered to Daemon’s black
dragon banner, and the red dragon battled

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:36.230
the black.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:42.150
The great houses, like the Lannisters, Arryns,
Tullys, and Martells, stayed loyal to the

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:46.570
Targaryens – they wanted to preserve their
power in the status quo.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:51.280
The Blackfyre supporters were mostly the less
powerful houses hoping to gain power under

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:56.430
a different king – houses like the Yronwoods
in Dorne, and the Reynes in the westerlands

00:06:56.430 --> 00:07:00.210
have a history of rebelling against their
liege lords.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:03.400
So there were “many battles” all across
Westeros.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.810
Fireball kicked some Lannister arse in the
westerlands.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:11.910
But just before the final battle, Fireball
was killed by some random archer – some

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:15.419
fans suspect that Bloodraven was behind this.

00:07:15.419 --> 00:07:20.460
But the First Blackfyre Rebellion ended at
the Battle of the Redgrass Field.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:26.610
Daemon Blackfyre fought brilliantly, and had
an epic duel with Gwayne Corbray of the Kingsguard.

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:31.760
Corbray had a Valyrian steel sword called
Lady Forlorn, and every time it clashed with

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:36.530
Blackfyre the sound could be heard from miles
around, [“half a song and half a scream”].

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:41.130
Daemon defeated Corbray, but then helped his
wounded enemy get to safety.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:46.000
Bloodraven took advantage of this moment to
rain arrows on his half-brother – weirwood

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.750
arrows, “driven as much by sorcery” as
by his bow.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:54.650
Daemon Blackfyre and two of his sons were
killed.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:08:00.210
Bittersteel took up Daemon’s sword and led
a “mad charge” to rally the rebels.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:04.760
Bloodraven fought a duel with Bittersteel,
and Bloodraven lost an eye.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:10.090
Then Prince Baelor Breakspear and Prince Maekar
crushed the rebel army, like a hammer and

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.630
an anvil.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:17.840
So Daemon Blackfyre was defeated – but some
of his sons and Bittersteel survived.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:22.979
They went across to Essos, and founded a mercenary
group called the Golden Company, made up of

00:08:22.979 --> 00:08:25.930
exiled lords and knights from Westeros.

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:29.990
They took contracts to fight all over the
east, but they never forgot their goal to

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:35.099
return to Westeros and put a Blackfyre on
the Throne.

00:08:35.099 --> 00:08:39.909
Back in Westeros, King Daeron punished the
lords who had rebelled against him.

00:08:39.909 --> 00:08:44.810
Rebels like Gormon Peake had some of their
lands and power taken away and their children

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:49.439
taken hostage, to stop them from rebelling
again.

00:08:49.439 --> 00:08:54.220
So it seemed that Daeron had cemented his
power, and as long as nothing terrible happened,

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:56.920
he would rule for many more years.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:59.180
But then something terrible happened.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:04.759
The heir to the throne Baelor Breakspear died
at a tournament, as told in story The Hedge

00:09:04.759 --> 00:09:05.759
Knight.

00:09:05.759 --> 00:09:12.300
Then a deadly plague hit Westeros, that killed
Baelor’s sons, and killed King Daeron.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:18.540
So the weak and bookish Aerys Targaryen became
king, and his reign was troubled by ironborn

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.699
raiders and drought.

00:09:20.699 --> 00:09:26.110
Bloodraven practically ruled the realm for
him, and was brutal in spying and executing

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:28.910
people for treasonous speech.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:30.839
Many people hated Bloodraven.

00:09:30.839 --> 00:09:36.089
And the recent plague had killed a lot of
the hostages held against rebel lords.

00:09:36.089 --> 00:09:42.720
So Gormon Peake saw these divided times as
an opportunity to win back his power and pride.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:48.649
He planned a second Blackfyre rebellion with
one of Daemon Blackfyre’s sons, Daemon the

00:09:48.649 --> 00:09:49.720
Second.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:54.490
With Lord Butterwell, they held a wedding
tournament to bring together Blackfyre supporters.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:10:00.189
Daemon was convinced he would succeed and
become king because he had prophetic dreams

00:10:00.189 --> 00:10:02.740
of a dragon egg hatching.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:08.110
But he didn’t have enough allies – Bittersteel
and the Golden Company didn’t support him,

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:12.959
possibly because Daemon was gay, or possibly
just because his plan sucked.

00:10:12.959 --> 00:10:18.480
Daemon’s magic dreams didn’t work out
like he hoped, and his plans were ruined by

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:23.779
Duncan the Tall, and the son of Fireball,
and some secret toilet dwarfs – it’s a

00:10:23.779 --> 00:10:26.179
whole thing, go watch our Mystery Knight video.

00:10:26.179 --> 00:10:32.740
The point is, the Second Blackfyre Rebellion
failed before it even began, and Bloodraven

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:34.970
imprisoned Daemon the Second.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:41.149
But after Daemon died, his brother Haegon
launched the Third Blackfyre Rebellion.

00:10:41.149 --> 00:10:46.149
Haegon Blackfyre, Bittersteel, and the Golden
Company attacked, and they were defeated by

00:10:46.149 --> 00:10:47.439
the Targaryens.

00:10:47.439 --> 00:10:52.910
We’re told that Prince Maekar showed “leadership”,
Prince Egg showed “courage”, and Prince

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:55.319
Aerion took.. “actions”.

00:10:55.319 --> 00:11:02.529
Aerion was mad and cruel, so whatever “actions”
he did may not have been.. helpful.

00:11:02.529 --> 00:11:05.579
Bloodraven fought another duel with Bittersteel.

00:11:05.579 --> 00:11:10.189
This was twenty years after the first rebellion,
and these guys were still fighting over who

00:11:10.189 --> 00:11:12.249
got to root their sister.

00:11:12.249 --> 00:11:17.660
This personal beef between the white dragon
Bloodraven and the red stallion Bittersteel,

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:24.309
the Blackwood and the Bracken, continued to
drive the conflict of the Blackfyre rebellions.

00:11:24.309 --> 00:11:29.639
Anyway the Blackfyres were defeated, and Haegon
was “slain treacherously” after he had

00:11:29.639 --> 00:11:34.619
surrendered, which sounds like something Bloodraven
might do, or maybe Aerion.

00:11:34.619 --> 00:11:38.679
We’re told almost nothing about the Third
Rebellion, so hopefully we’ll get the full

00:11:38.679 --> 00:11:41.529
story in a future Dunk &amp; Egg novella.

00:11:41.529 --> 00:11:46.910
We do know that Bittersteel was captured,
and Bloodraven wanted him killed, to finally

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.610
end his rebellions.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:53.950
But King Aerys chose to just send him to the
Night’s Watch on the Wall instead.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:59.899
This was “a foolish mercy”, because Bittersteel
just escaped, went back east, and prepared

00:11:59.899 --> 00:12:02.990
for the next Blackfyre rebellion.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:06.059
After King Aerys died, Maekar became king.

00:12:06.059 --> 00:12:09.559
When Maekar died, there was a big council
to choose the next king.

00:12:09.559 --> 00:12:14.800
They didn’t want Aerion’s son Maegor to
be king, because he was a baby, and his dad

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:15.800
was crazy.

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:20.259
They didn’t want Daeron’s daughter Vaella,
because she was “simple-minded”, and,

00:12:20.259 --> 00:12:21.399
a girl.

00:12:21.399 --> 00:12:25.369
Maester Aemon refused to be king, because
he was a maester.

00:12:25.369 --> 00:12:30.170
And they didn’t want Egg, because he grew
up travelling with a hedge knight called Dunk,

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:35.569
and Egg all these crazy ideas about how peasants
should have ‘rights’ and stuff.

00:12:35.569 --> 00:12:42.389
So then, a fifth option arrived – Aenys
Blackfyre, a younger son of Daemon the First,

00:12:42.389 --> 00:12:44.139
said that he should be king.

00:12:44.139 --> 00:12:49.620
Bloodraven promised to let Aenys come to King’s
Landing and speak unharmed, but Bloodraven

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:55.899
lied, and cut off Aenys’ head, ruthlessly
crushing a Blackfyre once again.

00:12:55.899 --> 00:12:59.730
And the council chose Egg to be king.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:04.889
As punishment for dishonourably killing Aenys,
King Egg sent Bloodraven to the Night’s

00:13:04.889 --> 00:13:06.399
Watch on the Wall.

00:13:06.399 --> 00:13:12.019
Years later, Bloodraven became the magical
three-eyed crow, and now continues to do morally

00:13:12.019 --> 00:13:17.420
questionable things for the sake of the greater
good – like turning Bran into a magic tree

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:18.420
boy.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:24.040
In Book 5, Bloodraven tells Bran that he once
had a brother that he loved, a brother that

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:26.989
he hated, and a woman he desired.

00:13:26.989 --> 00:13:32.029
The woman he desired was Shiera, the brother
he hated was Bittersteel.

00:13:32.029 --> 00:13:34.699
The brother he loved might have been Daeron.

00:13:34.699 --> 00:13:40.269
But maybe, in a way, Bloodraven loved his
brother Daemon – which would add a layer

00:13:40.269 --> 00:13:45.189
of tragedy to his killing of Daemon on the
Redgrass Field.

00:13:45.189 --> 00:13:50.230
Bloodraven does some terrible things in his
fight against the Blackfyres.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:52.079
He kills his brother Daemon.

00:13:52.079 --> 00:13:58.720
Runs a brutal surveillance state under King
Aerys, and captures Daemon the Second.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:02.300
Dishonourably kills Aenys, and possibly Haegon
as well.

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:06.160
Bloodraven argues that the ends justify the
means.

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:11.519
Traitors must be crushed, or else they’ll
just rebel again, so it’s worth sacrificing

00:14:11.519 --> 00:14:14.209
his honour for the sake of the realm.

00:14:14.209 --> 00:14:17.100
And it seems like Bloodraven’s right.

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:22.540
Like, King Aerys showed mercy to Bittersteel,
and that was “foolish”, cause Bittersteel

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.769
just went and rebelled again.

00:14:24.769 --> 00:14:29.199
Back when Daeron was king, he was friendly
to his rival Daemon, and even married him

00:14:29.199 --> 00:14:32.769
to the wife who bore his rebel sons.

00:14:32.769 --> 00:14:38.649
If Daeron had imprisoned or killed Daemon
instead, generations of Blackfyre rebellions

00:14:38.649 --> 00:14:40.269
might never have happened.

00:14:40.269 --> 00:14:45.870
“too much mercy” from the Targaryens led
to generations of war [“pain, grief, war,

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:46.870
and murder”].

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:50.319
Like how Ned Stark’s mercy just gets him
killed and leads to war.

00:14:50.319 --> 00:14:56.329
So is Bloodraven right, that mercy and honour
leads to conflict, and that only ruthless

00:14:56.329 --> 00:14:58.709
violence can keep you safe?

00:14:58.709 --> 00:15:02.139
Well the story’s not over yet.

00:15:02.139 --> 00:15:06.199
In the reign of King Egg, the Fourth Blackfyre
Rebellion began.

00:15:06.199 --> 00:15:11.929
Daemon the First’s grandson, Daemon Blackfyre
the Third, landed near King’s Landing, with

00:15:11.929 --> 00:15:17.540
Bittersteel and the Golden Company – but
few lords supported this rebellion.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:22.920
King Egg rode out to fight them, alongside
his sons – Jaehaerys, Daeron and Duncan

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:26.810
the Small – who was probably named after
Duncan the Tall.

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:32.369
At the Battle of Wendwater Bridge, Dunk killed
Daemon the Third, and the Blackfyres were

00:15:32.369 --> 00:15:39.110
defeated again, Bittersteel fled east again,
and a few years later Bittersteel died in

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:41.540
battle fighting as a mercenary.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:47.459
He was sixty-nine years old, and he died as
he lived – “with a sword in his hand and

00:15:47.459 --> 00:15:50.069
defiance upon his lips”.

00:15:50.069 --> 00:15:53.569
Bittersteel failed to get a Blackfyre on the
throne.

00:15:53.569 --> 00:15:56.009
But his legacy lives on.

00:15:56.009 --> 00:16:01.749
The Golden Company, and the surviving Blackfyres
continued to rebel in his name.

00:16:01.749 --> 00:16:06.510
The Golden Company gilded Bittersteel’s
skull, covered it with gold, and they still

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:11.489
carry it into battle on their banners, so
that one day, Bittersteel’s remains can

00:16:11.489 --> 00:16:14.360
return to Westeros to see a Blackfyre on the
Throne.

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:17.199
[Their war cry is “Beneath the gold, the
bitter steel” ].

00:16:17.199 --> 00:16:21.209
King Egg died in the mysterious tragedy of
Summerhall.

00:16:21.209 --> 00:16:27.439
Egg’s son Jaehaerys became king, and he
faced a new Blackfyre threat.

00:16:27.439 --> 00:16:30.649
Over in Essos, “nine outlaws, exiles, pirates,
and sellsword captains” [met “beneath

00:16:30.649 --> 00:16:35.549
the Tree of Crowns”, and] formed “an unholy
alliance”.

00:16:35.549 --> 00:16:41.220
The “Band of Nine”, or “Ninepenny Kings”,
were a motley group of badasses from around

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:44.509
the world who worked together to conquer.

00:16:44.509 --> 00:16:49.860
They included Derrick Fossoway, the Bad Apple
– a descendent of the Fossoways from The

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:50.860
Hedge Knight.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:56.819
There was Samarro Saan, an ancestor of the
pirate Salladhor Saan, from the main series.

00:16:56.819 --> 00:17:01.910
And there was “the last Blackfyre”, Maelys
the Monstrous.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:06.659
Maelys was “grotesquely huge”, strong,
and savage.

00:17:06.659 --> 00:17:12.170
He had supposedly eaten his twin brother in
the womb, so his brother’s tiny head grew

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.130
from his neck.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:19.709
Maelys took over the Golden Company by killing
his Blackfyre cousin – he killed his cousin’s

00:17:19.709 --> 00:17:25.470
horse with one punch, then ripped his cousin’s
head off his shoulders.

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:30.790
Maelys and the Ninepenny Kings and the Golden
Company took over Tyrosh and the Stepstones,

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:33.480
and prepared to attack Westeros.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:38.520
So King Jaehaerys sent an army to destroy
them, led by Ormund Baratheon.

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:44.429
Ormund was killed by Maelys, and he died in
the arms of his son Steffon – Steffon is

00:17:44.429 --> 00:17:48.539
the father of Robert, Stannis and Renly Baratheon.

00:17:48.539 --> 00:17:54.570
Lord Quellon Greyjoy, grandfather of Theon
and Asha, led a fleet of longships into battle.

00:17:54.570 --> 00:18:00.470
The Starks, Lannisters, Arryns, Tullys and
Martells also sent soldiers, so the gang wsall

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:04.070
here, united against the Ninepenny Kings.

00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:10.299
Many young knights won fame and glory in the
fighting, including Catelyn’s uncle, Brynden

00:18:10.299 --> 00:18:14.669
Blackfish, and Tywin Lannister, along with
his brothers Kevan and Tygett.

00:18:14.669 --> 00:18:19.570
During the war, Tywin and Steffon Baratheon
made friends with the king’s son, Aerys

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:25.950
Targaryen – but that friendship later broke
down when Aerys became the Mad King.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:30.809
Lord Hoster Tully made friends with a Lord
Baelish, so Baelish’s son Petyr went to

00:18:30.809 --> 00:18:36.399
live with the Tullys in Riverrun – the beginning
of Littlefinger’s rise to power.

00:18:36.399 --> 00:18:41.380
Jon Arryn made friends with Rickard Stark
and Steffon Baratheon, which eventually led

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:47.169
to the Arryn-Stark-Baratheon alliance that
took down the Mad King in Robert’s Rebellion.

00:18:47.169 --> 00:18:52.130
So a lot of the relationships that shaped
the past generation of the game of thrones

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:54.500
began in this war.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:19:00.590
The war ended when a young Barristan Selmy
cut a bloody path through the Golden Company

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:03.120
and killed Maelys the Monstrous.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:08.909
So after five generations of rebellions, House
Blackfyre was finally dead, and they’ll

00:19:08.909 --> 00:19:11.110
never be a threat again.

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:12.110
…Right?

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:16.690
We’re told that Maelys was “the last Blackfyre”.

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:22.140
But then we’re told that Maelys was just
the last Blackfyre through the male line,

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:27.850
which implies that some Blackfyres survived
through the female line – meaning, Daemon’s

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:31.539
daughters or granddaughters might’ve survived
and had kids.

00:19:31.539 --> 00:19:35.289
So maybe the Blackfyres could return.

00:19:35.289 --> 00:19:40.429
In the books, Varys and Illyrio’s secret
plan is make this kid Young Griff the King

00:19:40.429 --> 00:19:41.429
of Westeros.

00:19:41.429 --> 00:19:47.860
They say that Young Griff is Aegon Targaryen,
the son of Rhaegar and Elia, who was believed

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:52.220
to have died, but Varys claims they secretly
saved him.

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:57.100
Some characters don’t believe this kid is
really Aegon Targaryen.

00:19:57.100 --> 00:20:02.610
And in visions and prophecy, we’re warned
of a “false” dragon, or a “mummer’s

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:05.170
dragon”, meaning a fake Targaryen.

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:11.419
Varys was a mummer, or street performer, and
a master of illusion and deception.

00:20:11.419 --> 00:20:18.950
Varys says that “Power resides where men
believe it resides”, that power is a mummer’s

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:19.950
trick.

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:22.990
Young Griff is his “mummer’s dragon”.

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:24.830
So what’s the trick?

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:30.029
There’s a theory that the Young Griff is
not Aegon Targaryen – he’s actually a

00:20:30.029 --> 00:20:31.029
Blackfyre.

00:20:31.029 --> 00:20:36.630
Cause in Book 5, Young Griff invades Westeros
to take the Throne, calling himself Aegon

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.140
Targaryen.

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:41.660
And he’s supported by the Golden Company.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:47.140
For a hundred years, the Golden Company have
fought against the Targaryens for the Blackfyres.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:51.110
So Tyrion asks why would they fight for a
Targaryen?

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:57.059
And that’s when Illyrio says that the Blackfyres
are extinct through the male line.

00:20:57.059 --> 00:21:02.049
He says the Golden Company supports them because
of contracts writ in blood, “I say no more”.

00:21:02.049 --> 00:21:06.250
Illyrio and Varys made their alliance with
the Golden Company with Company commander

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:08.120
Blackheart Toyne.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:13.250
And the Toynes would have a particular grudge
against the Targaryens because the Targaryens

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.720
caused the downfall of their family a hundred
years ago.

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:24.930
It is so weird for the Golden Company to support
Young Griff – unless Young Griff is a Blackfyre.

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:27.500
This might also explain Illyrio’s motivations.

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:33.320
Cause Tyrion wonders why Illyrio is in this
conspiracy to make Young Griff the King of

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:34.380
Westeros.

00:21:34.380 --> 00:21:39.860
Illyrio is a cheese merchant from Essos, why
does he care about putting this teenager on

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.620
a foreign throne?

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:47.549
Illyrio says he’s just in it for the money,
but Tyrion thinks he has some deeper reason.

00:21:47.549 --> 00:21:52.399
Illyrio says he has “debts of affection
to repay”.

00:21:52.399 --> 00:21:57.929
Illyrio is very fond of Young Griff – he
wants to spend time with him, praises him,

00:21:57.929 --> 00:21:59.029
gives him gifts.

00:21:59.029 --> 00:22:03.050
He’s almost like a father to Young Griff.

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:08.490
Illyrio once had a wife called Serra, who
he loved deeply before she died.

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:14.710
And Serra had silver-gold hair like a Targaryen..
or like a Blackfyre.

00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:21.260
So the theory is that Serra was a Blackfyre,
and Young Griff was her son with Illyrio.

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:28.039
Illyrio wants Young Griff on the Iron Throne
to honour his beloved Serra Blackfyre.

00:22:28.039 --> 00:22:33.029
And it looks like Young Griff might actually
succeed where past generations of Blackfyres

00:22:33.029 --> 00:22:34.029
failed.

00:22:34.029 --> 00:22:39.649
Cause, in some ways, Young Griff is similar
to Daemon Blackfyre the Second – he’s

00:22:39.649 --> 00:22:42.190
young, handsome, and confident.

00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:47.149
He uses a fake name, and dyes his hair to
hide the Blackfyre blonde.

00:22:47.149 --> 00:22:53.640
But Daemon the Second failed because he didn’t
have an army, he didn’t have enough alliances,

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:58.000
and he didn’t have important symbols like
the sword Blackfyre.

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:01.330
Young Griff could soon have all three.

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:06.019
He has the Golden Company’s army, and they’ve
already taken castles in the stormlands.

00:23:06.019 --> 00:23:10.830
He’s working on an alliance with Dorne,
and has “friends in the Reach”.

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:15.180
As for the sword Blackfyre, its location is
a mystery.

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:20.010
But in a draft of a chapter read by George
Martin, Illyrio says he has a gift for Young

00:23:20.010 --> 00:23:23.100
Griff, and mentions a “sword”.

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:27.890
So some fans believe that Illyrio has the
sword Blackfyre, and will give it to Young

00:23:27.890 --> 00:23:36.029
Griff, to show his legitimacy as king – and
to subtly hint at his Blackfyre heritage.

00:23:36.029 --> 00:23:39.250
Young Griff might just win the Iron Throne.

00:23:39.250 --> 00:23:44.740
But when Daenerys finally arrives, blazing
in from the east with her dragons, she’s

00:23:44.740 --> 00:23:48.340
gonna want Young Griff off her chair.

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:53.169
In Daenerys’ vision of the “mummer’s
dragon”, Daenerys is called the “slayer

00:23:53.169 --> 00:23:54.990
of lies”.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:00.000
Maybe she’ll slay the lie that Young Griff
is a Targaryen, and will destroy this false

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.179
king, finally truly ending House Blackfyre.

00:24:03.179 --> 00:24:07.650
But, if that’s what happens, what’s the
meaning here?

00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:12.791
Is the whole Blackfyre plotline, and Young
Griff, just one last obstacle between Daenerys

00:24:12.791 --> 00:24:14.669
and the Throne?

00:24:14.669 --> 00:24:19.700
Is the “mummer’s dragon” only there
“to give the heroes something to fight”,

00:24:19.700 --> 00:24:21.610
as Daenerys says?

00:24:21.610 --> 00:24:24.940
Maybe this could tie back to the theme of
mercy.

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:30.169
Like, all throughout the Blackfyre rebellions,
Bloodraven has argued that mercy is stupid

00:24:30.169 --> 00:24:32.789
and you should brutally kill your enemies.

00:24:32.789 --> 00:24:37.340
But maybe this time, brutal murder would be
a bad idea?

00:24:37.340 --> 00:24:42.559
Like, Young Griff might be seen as a popular
legitimate Targaryen king [“amidst a cheering

00:24:42.559 --> 00:24:43.559
crowd”].

00:24:43.559 --> 00:24:48.590
So if Daenerys the scary dragon lady incinerates
him in front of everyone, that could backfire

00:24:48.590 --> 00:24:51.960
on her, even if Daenerys is right.

00:24:51.960 --> 00:24:55.919
Maybe this time, mercy to the Blackfyres would
be wise.

00:24:55.919 --> 00:25:02.809
And maybe being right, and having the true
Targaryen bloodline, isn’t what’s important.

00:25:02.809 --> 00:25:07.300
Maybe it doesn’t matter whether Young Griff
is a Targaryen or a Blackfyre.

00:25:07.300 --> 00:25:11.480
“Power resides where men believe it resides”.

00:25:11.480 --> 00:25:14.259
And “Treason … is only a word”.

00:25:14.259 --> 00:25:19.990
This whole hundred-year conflict traces back
to whether Daeron or Daemon was the true heir

00:25:19.990 --> 00:25:21.509
of King Aegon.

00:25:21.509 --> 00:25:25.100
And for all we know, Daemon might have been
right.

00:25:25.100 --> 00:25:29.720
Maybe Naerys really did cheat on Aegon with
their brother, and Daemon was the rightful

00:25:29.720 --> 00:25:31.509
king all along.

00:25:31.509 --> 00:25:38.160
But why should a question of who porked who
a hundred years ago cause generations of war?

00:25:38.160 --> 00:25:43.129
Jorah once told Daenerys that the common people
don’t care whether they’re ruled by “a

00:25:43.129 --> 00:25:47.360
true king or a usurper” – they just want
to be “left in peace”.

00:25:47.360 --> 00:25:53.379
But the idea of monarchy where the Throne
is inherited by the king’s trueborn heir

00:25:53.379 --> 00:25:59.520
has caused wars for centuries, and another
Targaryen-Blackfyre conflict would just continue

00:25:59.520 --> 00:26:01.610
this cycle of violence.

00:26:01.610 --> 00:26:07.700
So maybe the Throne should be destroyed in
the end, along with the Targaryens and Blackfyres,

00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:09.879
trueborn and falseborn.

00:26:09.879 --> 00:26:13.370
So that a different a kind of king can rule.

00:26:13.370 --> 00:26:17.080
Bran Stark won’t have kids, trueborn or
bastard.

00:26:17.080 --> 00:26:22.440
There won’t be wars to inherit his throne,
so long as keeps ruling for centuries, with

00:26:22.440 --> 00:26:28.350
immortality from the weirwoods, like his master
Bloodraven.

00:26:28.350 --> 00:26:35.020
The magic of the weirwoods and the three-eyed
crow is super creepy and controlling.

00:26:35.020 --> 00:26:40.250
If Bran becomes king in the books, he might
just be a puppet of Bloodraven and the old

00:26:40.250 --> 00:26:41.250
gods.

00:26:41.250 --> 00:26:47.279
So after a hundred years, and six Blackfyre
rebellions, King Bran would be Bloodraven’s

00:26:47.279 --> 00:26:51.910
victory in his ancient rivalry with Bittersteel
and the Blackfyres [and Brackens].

00:26:51.910 --> 00:26:57.440
He might even get Shiera back in the end – there’s
a theory that she’s still alive as the masked

00:26:57.440 --> 00:26:59.470
sorceress Quaithe.

00:26:59.470 --> 00:27:01.399
But that’s all just speculation.

00:27:01.399 --> 00:27:04.420
We don’t know how the books will end.

00:27:04.420 --> 00:27:08.520
We don’t know if Bran will be king in the
books, and we don’t know for sure if Young

00:27:08.520 --> 00:27:10.409
Griff if is a Blackfyre.

00:27:10.409 --> 00:27:15.830
But the history of the Blackfyre rebellions
explores the story’s big themes of power,

00:27:15.830 --> 00:27:23.220
mercy, and monarchy, and they could be an
important part of the endgame of A Song of

00:27:23.220 --> 00:27:24.389
Ice and Fire.

00:27:24.389 --> 00:27:28.600
If you watched this video, and you haven’t
read A Song of Ice and Fire,.. you should

00:27:28.600 --> 00:27:29.600
do that.

00:27:29.600 --> 00:27:34.389
As well as the main five books, there’s
the Dunk &amp; Egg novellas, and the history books.

